   <%- include("partials/schema") %>
   <script type="application/ld+json">
   {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Home",
      "url": "https://printfromweb.onrender.com",
      "description": "Transfer files to another device with a printer connected to it and print from browser right away. Totally free. No account, no external app, tracking or ads.",
      "dateModified": "2026-06-23T14:30:00+00:00"
   }
   </script>
   <script>
      window.onload = () => {
         const successfulTransferText = document.getElementById("transferred-files-count");
         document.querySelectorAll("span#current-year").forEach(span => {
            span.textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
         });
         const server = new WebSocket(`wss://${location.host}`);
         server.onmessage = (event) => {
            const message = JSON.parse(event.data)
            successfulTransferText.textContent = message.value;
         }
      }
   </script>
   <title>Print from your phone online - Print From Web</title>
</head>
<body>
   
   <%- include("partials/navbar", { privacy: false }) %>
   <main class="centered-content">
      <div id="introduction">
         <h1>Web based tool for file transfer + print:</h1>
         <hr>
         <p>Print from Web is a web based tool, through which you can transfer a document to another device and get the file opened in the receiver's browser, ready to print. This tool is very useful to you if your printer is not a network printer and you don't use any application for file sharing, and neither a compatible usb cable. Also useful if you want to send a document to someone else who can print it for you without them having to save it in their device.</p>
         <p>How did I get this idea? Well, I have all of the problems I just mentioned.</p>
         <p>Works well enough to transfer PDFs, another good thing is that the files aren't stored anywhere in the server side.</p>
         <h2>Get started:</h2>
         <hr>
         <p>
            <ul>
               <li>First, the sender needs to create a connection ID for the transfer first.</li>
               <li>Then, the receiver can join the connection with the ID.</li>
               <li>Once the receiver joins, the sender can select the file and send it.</li>
            </ul>
         </p>
      </div>
      <div id="options">
         <a href="/send"><button>Send</button></a>
         <a href="/receive"><button>Receive</button></a>
      </div>
      <div class="centered-content" style="flex-direction: column;">
         <p>Total files transferred online:</p>
         <p id="transferred-files-count"></p>
      </div>
      <div id="how-to-use">
         <h2>How to use:</h2>
         <hr>
         <ol>
            <li>
               <p>First click on "Connect as Sender", (or ask the sender to connect).</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>In the next page, sender has to create a connection, a room ID is given to sender.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>Sender shares the room ID with receiver.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>Receiver has to choose "Connect as Receiver" in the home page:</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>In the next page, type the room ID in the input box and press connect button to connect to sender.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>Sender can now select files and send it.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
               <p>If receiver cannot see the popup, they can open popup menu and click on the blob link to the document.</p>
            </li>
         </ol>
      </div>
   </main>
   <%- include("partials/footer") %>
</body>
</html>